target:    tests/oracle/classify.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
expect:    P48-a-pin-on-the-other-arm-only-is-not-a-pin-either
kind:      guard-removal
rationale: BOTH arms must be pinned for a window to be pinned: a window pinned on one side only leaves
           the other free to move, so a difference cannot be attributed to the code. The `and` is
           what says so. S4-pin-reads-as-or-01 covers `and` becoming `or`; this covers the OLD
           side being dropped entirely, which the same asymmetric-plant gap left undefended.
---
--- a/tests/oracle/classify.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/classify.py
@@ -612,7 +612,7 @@
                   for name in ("clock_dependent", "calendar_day_dependent")),
         # BOTH arms must be pinned for the pin to help. A window pinned on one side only leaves
         # the other free to move, which is the state the pin exists to prevent.
-        pinned=_flag(old_env, "pinned") and _flag(new_env, "pinned"),
+        pinned=_flag(new_env, "pinned"),
         observable=observable,
         register_hit=hit,
         register_near=tuple(near),
